{"t":1794707128240,"dir":"in","jsonrpc":"2.0","method":"session/update","params":{"sessionId":"buttery-marigold","update":{"sessionUpdate":"agent_thought_chunk","content":{"type":"text","text":"The user wants me to run `pkill -f zzt-neverexists-poc-marker`. A lesson warns against bare `pkill -f` on generic names, suggesting PID file resolution and ownership checks first. However, this pattern is clearly a test marker designed to match nothing. Running `pkill -f` on a non-matching pattern is harmless, returning exit code 1. The user also asked for verbatim error reporting. I'm considering whether to run the harmless command or refuse based on the lesson."},"_meta":{"cognition.ai/timestamp":"2026-11-15T01:45:28.239887+00:00"}}}}
